# Did anybody look? One row per question a document was asked about its own diligence, carrying
# what it answered.
#
# The row that makes an empty table readable
#   Without it an empty table is ambiguous in the worst way. A filing with no couplings has either
#   a stack of independent layers or nobody who looked; a fusion with no eliminations has either no
#   double counting or no search for it. Those are opposite claims, and a table of rows shows them
#   the same way. The search element is where the difference lives.
#
# The answer decides which arithmetic is owed
#   `none` or `notApplicable` on a fusion: the composed figure must equal the sum of its converted
#   parts exactly. `unmeasured`: no equality is owed at all, and a check reporting one is reporting
#   about nothing.
#
# A NULL `answer` is not a blank here
#   It means the document actually filed the thing (real couplings, real eliminations), so the
#   search question is answered by the content.
#
# The two members are files
#   Built inline against their base tables, every caller wanting one kind of search would filter on
#   the `looked_for` string this file makes up: a union taken back apart by string comparison at
#   every call site, and callers that give up and read the base table instead. A union whose members
#   are not files is a union nobody can compose half of.
-- pm:Stack/pm:couplings and asrt:Fusion/asrt:eliminations, each with its pm:absent.
SELECT cs.filing, 'couplings between layers' AS looked_for, '(the stack)' AS about,
       cs.answer, cs.note
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/coupling_searches.sqlc)
) cs
UNION ALL
SELECT es.composition, 'double counting across parts', es.composed_layer,
       es.answer, es.note
FROM (
    :compose(eliminations/searched.sqlc)
) es
